        {
          "kicker": "TABLE PRESSURE",
          "heading": "Interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula seeks improvement with Fiji bottom of the table",
          "body": "Fiji occupies 12th place in the Nations Championship standings after three matches, following a 17-33 defeat to Scotland in the previous round. Under interim head coach Senirusi Seruvakula, the side has registered 49 points and conceded 145 across the tournament so far, leaving them with a points difference of -96. While the Flying Fijians reached a record world ranking of No. 7 in 2023, the squad is currently the only winless side in the competition."
