    "387": {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "SELECTION LEAK",
          "heading": "Jean-Marc Lhermet defends France's leaked elite player list following public uproar",
          "body": "A leaked resource-sharing agreement between the FFR and LNR has caused friction across the Top 14 after Midi-Olympique published a secret list of 33 \"premium\" players. The deal restricts these individuals to nine internationals per season and mandates regular rest periods to prioritise the national side. FFR vice-president Jean-Marc Lhermet was forced to justify the metrics after fans questioned the absence of Grégory Alldritt and Maxime Lucu. Toulouse are set to be the hardest hit, with 13 players reportedly included on the protected roster."
        },
