    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match report",
          "heading": "Scott Bemand rues massive collapse as Ireland women surrender 19-point lead",
          "body": "Ireland women’s head coach Scott Bemand admitted his side \"should have won\" Sunday’s WXV opener after surrendering a 19-point lead against the USA. Despite scoring six tries at Tallaght Stadium, the hosts collapsed during the final quarter as the Eagles scored four unanswered tries to overturn a 31-12 deficit. Bemand criticised a second-half loss of discipline and technical control that allowed the visitors to snatch a 40-36 victory. Ireland must now regroup before facing Japan in Galway to keep their WXV campaign alive."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
