      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV OPENER",
          "heading": "Italy Women crush Japan Women as Vittoria Ostuni Minuzzi earns 50th cap",
          "body": "Italy Women secured their largest-ever victory over Japan Women with a dominant 55-21 win to open their WXV Global Series campaign. After an early scare saw the Sakura XV take a brief lead, the Azzurre responded with five first-half tries, including clinical efforts from Alyssa D'Inca and Vittoria Vecchini. The Italy captain marked her 50th cap with a second-half score as the Italians outplayed their opponents in all facets at Stadio Omero Tognon."
        },
